Chile: pioneer in responsible labelling
In 2010, Chile discovered that 60 percent of its population was overweight and that 25 percent of children under six years of age suffered from obesity, making the problem of malnutrition due to excess the country’s main public health concern. Faced with this issue, a group of parliamentarians led by Senator Guido Girardi asked itself the question: What determines people’s food habits and nutritional status? There is no simple answer. They are determined by multiple factors and one of the most influential is the food environment, including marketing and advertisement, the information available and nutrition labelling. That is where Chile wanted to make a difference.
